specific error message, it just won’t go through. What should I try next?","native_cost":0.0,"participant":"user_simulator","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"user","sequence":9,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T15:08:05.177388","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":[],"tool_error":null,"turn_index":9,"usage":{"completion_tokens":40,"prompt_tokens":2536}},{"content":"Thank you for checking. Let’s start by making sure your phone has the necessary service and data connectivity for MMS. Please follow these steps:\n\n1. Check your phone’s status bar and let me know:\n   - Do you see any signal bars (indicating cellular service)?\n   - Is mobile data enabled (look for a 4G, 5G, LTE, or similar icon)?\n   - Is Airplane Mode turned off?\n\nIf you’re not sure, I can guide you through how to check these on your device. Would you like instructions for checking your status bar, or do you already know how to do this?","native_cost":0.0,"participant":"evaluated_agent","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"assistant","sequence":10,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T15:08:06.769911","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":[],"tool_error":null,"turn_index":10,"usage":{"completion_tokens":129,"prompt_tokens":6773}},{"content":null,"native_cost":0.0,"participant":"user_simulator","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"user","sequence":11,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T15:08:07.802653","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":[{"arguments":{},"id":"call_44cgvu1VLb945ocYRLVTRatg","name":"check_status_bar","requestor":"user_simulator"}],"tool_error":null,"turn_index":11,"usage":{"completion_tokens":12,"prompt_tokens":2709}},{"content":"Status Bar: 📶¹ Poor | 2G | 📵 Data Disabled | 🔋 80%","native_cost":null,"participant":"tool_environment","reasoning":null,"requestor":"user_simulator","role":"tool","sequence":12,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T15:08:07.803074","tool_call_id":"call_44cgvu1VLb945ocYRLVTRatg","tool_calls":[],"tool_error":false,"turn_index":12,"usage":null},{"content":"I checked my status bar, and here’s what I see:\n- I have poor signal (just one bar).\n- It shows 2G.\n- Mobile data is disabled.\n- Airplane mode is off.\n\nWhat should I do next?","native_cost":0.0,"participant":"user_simulator","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"user","sequence":13,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T15:08:09.123832","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":[],"tool_error":null,"turn_index":13,"usage":{"completion_tokens":51,"prompt_tokens":2749}},{"content":"Thank you for the details. Here’s what we need to address:\n\n1. Your phone is connected to a 2G network, which is not suitable for MMS.\n2. Mobile data is disabled, and MMS requires mobile data to be enabled.\n\nLet’s start by enabling mobile data on your phone. Please turn on mobile data in your device settings. Once you’ve done that, let me know, and I’ll guide you to switch your network mode to a faster connection (like 4G or 5G), which is necessary for MMS to work properly.","native_cost":0.0,"participant":"evaluated_agent","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"assistant","sequence":14,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T15:08:10.877188","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":[],"tool_error":null,"turn_index":14,"usage":{"completion_tokens":116,"prompt_tokens":6957}},{"content":null,"native_cost":0.0,"participant":"user_simulator","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"user","sequence":15,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T15:08:12.058426","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":[{"arguments":{},"id":"call_3T7wPDco1K65LSCNdpbHm46j","name":"toggle_data","requestor":"user_simulator"}],"tool_error":null,"turn_index":15,"usage":{"completion_tokens":11,"prompt_tokens":2920}},{"content":"Mobile Data is now ON.\nStatus Bar: 📶¹ Poor | 2G | 📱 Data Enabled | 🔋 80%","native_cost":null,"participant":"tool_environment","reasoning":null,"requestor":"user_simulator","role":"tool","sequence":16,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T15:08:12.058948","tool_call_id":"call_3T7wPDco1K65LSCNdpbHm46j","tool_calls":[],"tool_error":false,"turn_index":16,"usage":null},{"content":"I’ve turned on mobile data. The status bar now shows data is enabled, but I’m still on a 2G network with poor signal. What should I do next?","native_cost":0.0,"participant":"user_simulator","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"user","sequence":17,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T15:08:13.502532","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":[],"tool_error":null,"turn_index":17,"usage":{"completion_tokens":38,"prompt_tokens":2964}},{"content":"Great, you’ve enabled mobile data. The next step is to change your network mode to prefer 4G or 5G, as 2G is not suitable for MMS.\n\nPlease go to your phone’s network settings and set the network mode to “4G/5G preferred” (or a similar option, such as “LTE/5G/4G auto”). After you make this change, check your status bar again and let me know if you see a 4G, LTE, or 5G icon and if your signal improves. \n\nIf you need step-by-step instructions for changing the network mode, let me know your phone model and I can guide you.","native_cost":0.0,"participant":"evaluated_agent","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"assistant","sequence":18,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T15:08:15.112343","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":[],"tool_error":null,"turn_index":18,"usage":{"completion_tokens":141,"prompt_tokens":7115}},{"content":null,"native_cost":0.0,"participant":"user_simulator","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"user","sequence":19,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T15:08:16.139695","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":[{"arguments":{"mode":"4g_5g_preferred"},"id":"call_MSe64xTsqH89XNVLHTplGea5","name":"set_network_mode_preference","requestor":"user_simulator"}],"tool_error":null,"turn_index":19,"usage":{"completion_tokens":24,"prompt_tokens":3147}},{"content":"Preferred Network Mode set to: 4g_5g_preferred\nStatus Bar: 📶⁴ Excellent | 5G | 📱 Data Enabled | 🔋 80%","native_cost":null,"participant":"tool_environment","reasoning":null,"requestor":"user_simulator","role":"tool","sequence":20,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T15:08:16.139968","tool_call_id":"call_MSe64xTsqH89XNVLHTplGea5","tool_calls":[],"tool_error":false,"turn_index":20,"usage":null},{"content":"I changed the network mode to “4G/5G preferred.” Now my status bar shows excellent signal strength and I’m connected to 5G with mobile data enabled. What should I do next?","native_cost":0.0,"participant":"user_simulator","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"user","sequence":21,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T15:08:17.689020","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":[],"tool_error":null,"turn_index":21,"usage":{"completion_tokens":43,"prompt_tokens":3218}},{"content":"That’s excellent progress! Now that you have a strong 5G connection and mobile data enabled, please try sending an MMS message again using your messaging app.\n\nLet me know if the MMS goes through successfully or if you still experience any issues. If it still doesn’t work, I’ll guide you through the next troubleshooting steps.","native_cost":0.0,"participant":"evaluated_agent","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"assistant","sequence":22,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T15:08:19.075763","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":[],"tool_error":null,"turn_index":22,"usage":{"completion_tokens":68,"prompt_tokens":7303}},{"content":null,"native_cost":0.0,"participant":"user_simulator","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"user","sequence":23,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T15:08:20.323096","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":[{"arguments":{},"id":"call_KzENk5V8WJc6FozHoJjqy9QP","name":"can_send_mms","requestor":"user_simulator"}],"tool_error":null,"turn_index":23,"usage":{"completion_tokens":13,"prompt_tokens":3333}},{"content":"Your messaging app cannot send MMS messages.","native_cost":null,"participant":"tool_environment","reasoning":null,"requestor":"user_simulator","role":"tool","sequence":24,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T15:08:20.323477","tool_call_id":"call_KzENk5V8WJc6FozHoJjqy9QP","tool_calls":[],"tool_error":false,"turn_index":24,"usage":null},{"content":"I tried sending an MMS again, but it still won’t go through. It’s a bit frustrating since everything looks good with the signal and data now. What should I try next?","native_cost":0.0,"participant":"user_simulator","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"user","sequence":25,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T15:08:21.924737","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":[],"tool_error":null,"turn_index":25,"usage":{"completion_tokens":39,"prompt_tokens":3361}},{"content":"Thank you for your patience. Since your signal and data are now good but MMS still isn’t working, the next step is to check your phone’s APN (Access Point Name) settings, as incorrect APN settings are a common cause of MMS issues.\n\nPlease check your APN settings and let me know if you see an MMSC (Multimedia Messaging Service Center) URL listed. If you’re unsure how to check this, I can provide instructions based on your phone model. Would you like step-by-step guidance for checking your APN settings?","native_cost":0.0,"participant":"evaluated_agent","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"assistant","sequence":26,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T15:08:24.152312","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":[],"tool_error":null,"turn_index":26,"usage":{"completion_tokens":113,"prompt_tokens":7414}},{"content":null,"native_cost":0.0,"participant":"user_simulator","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"user","sequence":27,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T15:08:25.205040","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":[{"arguments":{},"id":"call_Y3z2kM8DfrcI5UV6vcV5jR2l","name":"check_apn_settings","requestor":"user_simulator"}],"tool_error":null,"turn_index":27,"usage":{"completion_tokens":13,"prompt_tokens":3517}},{"content":"Current APN Name: internet\nMMSC URL (for picture messages): http://mms.carrier.com/mms/wapenc\n(These are technical settings, usually best left unchanged.)","native_cost":null,"participant":"tool_environment","reasoning":null,"requestor":"user_simulator","role":"tool","sequence":28,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T15:08:25.205558","tool_call_id":"call_Y3z2kM8DfrcI5UV6vcV5jR2l","tool_calls":[],"tool_error":false,"turn_index":28,"usage":null},{"content":"I checked my APN settings. The APN name is set to “internet” and the MMSC URL is “http://mms.carrier.com/mms/wapenc.” Is there anything else I should look for, or do these settings seem correct?","native_cost":0.0,"participant":"user_simulator","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"user","sequence":29,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T15:08:27.292059","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":[],"tool_error":null,"turn_index":29,"usage":{"completion_tokens":55,"prompt_tokens":3576}},{"content":"Thank you for providing your APN details. The APN name and MMSC URL you listed appear to be in the correct format. Since your APN settings seem correct, let’s check a few more things that can affect MMS:\n\n1. Is Wi-Fi Calling enabled on your device? If so, please try turning it off and then attempt to send an MMS again.\n2. Does your messaging app have permission to access storage and SMS? This is necessary for sending MMS.\n\nCould you please check if Wi-Fi Calling is enabled and let me know? If you’re not sure how to check, I can guide you through the process.","native_cost":0.0,"participant":"evaluated_agent","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"assistant","sequence":30,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T15:08:29.262080","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":[],"tool_error":null,"turn_index":30,"usage":{"completion_tokens":130,"prompt_tokens":7586}},{"content":null,"native_cost":0.0,"participant":"user_simulator","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"user","sequence":31,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"